## Security Best Practices

### **Sensitive Data Storage**
```javascript
// ✅ Good - Use secure storage for sensitive data
import AsyncStorage from '@react-native-async-storage/async-storage';

const storeSecureData = async (key, value) => {
  try {
    await AsyncStorage.setItem(key, JSON.stringify(value));
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Storage error:', error);
  }
};
```

### **Input Validation**
```javascript
// ✅ Good - Validate user input
const validateEmail = (email) => {
  const emailRegex = /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/;
  return emailRegex.test(email);
};

const handleLogin = () => {
  if (!validateEmail(email)) {
    showError('INVALID_EMAIL');
    return;
  }
  
  // 繼續登入流程
};
```

## Testing Considerations

### **Component Testing**
```javascript
// ✅ Good - Write testable components
const BettingCard = ({ game, onBet }) => {
  const handleBet = () => {
    if (onBet) {
      onBet(game.id);
    }
  };

  return (
    <TouchableOpacity testID="betting-card" onPress={handleBet}>
      <Text testID="game-title">{game.title}</Text>
    </TouchableOpacity>
  );
};
```

## Common Anti-Patterns to Avoid

### **❌ Don't Do**
```javascript
// Don't use inline styles for static styles
<View style={{ padding: 16, backgroundColor: '#fff' }}>

// Don't forget to handle loading states
const fetchData = async () => {
  const data = await Api.getData(); // Missing loading states
  setData(data);
};

// Don't use direct state mutation
setState(state.push(newItem)); // Mutates state directly

// Don't forget platform-specific considerations
<Button title="登入" /> // May look different on iOS vs Android
```

### **✅ Do This Instead**
```javascript
// Use StyleSheet for static styles
<View style={styles.container}>

// Handle loading states properly
const fetchData = async () => {
  setLoading(true);
  try {
    const data = await Api.getData();
    setData(data);
  } catch (error) {
    handleError(error);
  } finally {
    setLoading(false);
  }
};

// Use immutable state updates
setState([...state, newItem]);

// Consider platform-specific styling
<TouchableOpacity style={styles.button}>
  <Text>登入</Text>
</TouchableOpacity>
```

